    "findings": "Before the change the saved-session path returns 409, so failure rendering and battle rendering are different endpoints. Compare completed no-solo controls separately. Normal admission and reentry retain their SQL counts. Saved progress adds a guarded snapshot write, plus a row lock in Postgres. No rendering-loop changes. First loads span asset fetch/decoding and main-thread work; the post-mount loaded handler is only part of that time. WebKit reports long frames and an existing ResizeObserver warning. No claimed speedup.",
